What is a Diamond Package Substrate?
Diamond Package Substrates serve as a high‑performance thermal interface and interconnect medium in advanced semiconductor packages. The intrinsic thermal conductivity of natural or synthetic diamond-up to 2200 W/mK-provides a heat‑spreading capability far superior to conventional ceramic or metal‑nitride solutions. In addition, diamond’s wide band‑gap and low dielectric loss make it an ideal electrically insulating carrier for frequency‑critical RF and microwave modules. The material’s exceptional hardness and coefficient of thermal expansion (CTE) closely match that of silicon carbide (SiC) and gallium nitride (GaN), allowing reliable co‑packaging of power devices that operate under demanding thermal‑cycling conditions.

